  "abstract": "Perl is a high-level programming language that is commonly used for system\nadministration utilities and web programming. The perl516 packages provide a\nrecent stable release of Perl with a number of additional utilities, scripts,\nand database connectors for MySQL and PostgreSQL.\n\nThe perl516 packages have been upgraded to a later version that is required by\nRed Hat Software Collections 1.1, which provides a number of bug fixes and\nenhancements over the previous version.\n\nThe perl-Module-Pluggable packages have been upgraded to upstream version 5.1,\nwhich provides a number of bug fixes over the previous version, for example,\nplug-ins with a single letter name are now correctly located by the\n\"Module::Pluggable\" module. (BZ#1059119)\n\nThe perl-version packages have been upgraded to upstream version 0.99.07, which\nprovides a number of enhancements over the previous version, for example, the\npackages now include the \"version::vpp\" and \"version::regex\" modules.\n(BZ#1059183)\n\nThis update also fixes the following bugs:\n\n* Lists of build-time or runtime \"requires\" have been updated in several perl516\npackages. (BZ#1009503, BZ#1009507, BZ#1009514, BZ#1064743, BZ#1066077,\nBZ#1066320, BZ#1066455)\n\n* Filters of runtime \"provides\" and \"requires\" have been fixed in several\nperl516 packages. (BZ#1037448, BZ#1038132, BZ#1040848, BZ#1040866, BZ#1063206,\nBZ#1064855)\n\nIn addition, this update adds the following enhancements:\n\n* The mod_perl extension has been added to the perl516 Software Collection. The\nextension enables full usage of the Perl programming language together with the\nApache httpd 2.4 web server. For example, with mod_perl, Perl can be used to\nmanage Apache httpd and respond to requests for web pages. (BZ#1033074)\n\n* The following files have been included in the perl516-runtime packages: the\nLICENCE file, the README file, and the perl516(7) manual page, which is located\nin the /opt/rh/ directory and contains description, usage, and examples related\nto the perl516 Software Collection. (BZ#1061453)\n\n* The perl-DateTime packages have been added to the perl516 Software Collection.\nThe included version 1.06 fixes several bugs, for example, the set_locale() and\nset_formatter() functions no longer corrupt underlying UTC time if the object\nhas ambiguous local time, such as daylight saving time. Further, the \"9**9**9\"\nexpression to define infinity now returns the correct result on the PowerPC SPE\n(Signal Processing Engine) and other platforms. (BZ#1018050, BZ#1058359)\n\nUsers of perl516 are advised to upgrade to these updated packages, which fix\nthese bugs and add these enhancements.\n",
